From c5701c33d095718eb9bb20a4150428a5ef9cbaa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:34:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] input: Adds support for wlr-virtual-pointer-unstable-v1
 protocol.

Creates the virtual pointer manager in the input manager. New virtual
pointers are added through the same path as backend input devices (now
factored into _wlmim_add_input_device), and mapped to the output that
the client suggests, if any.

Used by remote desktop servers (eg. wayvnc) and input automation tools.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
---
 doc/FEATURES.md     |  4 ++
 doc/protocols.md    |  8 ++++
 src/input/manager.c | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/FEATURES.md b/doc/FEATURES.md
index f9c2d97..ccd047b 100644
